<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <Version>1.0.7</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>1.0.7 - A zero-row write now throws the same exception any other provider would. VistaDB does not pre-reject a constraint or cascade violation the way SQL Server does; it silently affects no rows, so a genuine concurrency conflict and a refused write arrived looking identical and both were reported as a plain DbUpdateException, meaning a real conflict could not be caught as one. The two are now told apart by checking whether the targeted rows still match their conditions. 1.0.6 - Writes no longer report phantom concurrency conflicts. The generator ended every statement with SELECT @@ROWCOUNT, which is not a supported VistaDB expression (only @@IDENTITY, @@VERSION and @@TRANCOUNT are documented) and which 6.6.0 records as miscounting in multi-statement batches; a row that had been written came back as "expected to affect 1 row(s), but actually affected 0". Plain writes now emit the bare statement and take the count from ExecuteNonQuery, which is reliable. Genuine conflicts are still detected. 1.0.5 - Boolean column defaults now work in DDL. The bit mapping renders CAST(0 AS bit), which VistaDB accepts in a query but rejects in a DEFAULT clause (error 285, taking the ALTER TABLE down with error 120); booleans are written as bare 0/1 in migrations only. 1.0.4 - Boolean columns now work in queries. VistaDB has no boolean type and rejects a bare bit column where a condition is expected (error 666), so a search-condition converter, ported from the SQL Server provider, runs after all other SQL processing. 1.0.3 - Fix migrations: the history-table existence probe used INFORMATION_SCHEMA, which VistaDB rejects (error 627), and the create-if-not-exists script was unconditional, so every restart after the first failed with a duplicate table name.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Description>VistaDB database provider for Entity Framework Core.</Description>
    <AssemblyName>Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.VistaDB</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.VistaDB</RootNamespace>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);EF9100;CS1591</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Using Include="System.Data.Common" />
    <Using Include="System.Diagnostics" />
    <Using Include="System.Linq.Expressions" />
    <Using Include="System.Reflection" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.ChangeTracking" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Infrastructure" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Metadata" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Metadata.Builders" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Metadata.Conventions" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Metadata.Conventions.Infrastructure" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Migrations" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Migrations.Operations" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Query" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Scaffolding" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Storage" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Storage.ValueConversion" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Update" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.ValueGeneration" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Utilities" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging" />
    <Using Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Placeholder files for unsupported SqlServer types. The class bodies are wholly commented
    under "VistaDB: no analog —" markers. Excluded so they don't break abstract-base contracts.
    Remove the exclusions when reviving any of these mappings.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Remove="Storage\Internal\VistaDBSqlVariantTypeMapping.cs" />
    <Compile Remove="Storage\Internal\VistaDBStructuralJsonTypeMapping.cs" />
    <Compile Remove="Storage\Internal\VistaDBUdtTypeMapping.cs" />
    <Compile Remove="Storage\Internal\VistaDBVectorTypeMapping.cs" />
    <Compile Remove="ValueGeneration\Internal\VistaDBSequenceHiLoValueGenerator.cs" />
    <Compile Remove="ValueGeneration\Internal\VistaDBSequenceValueGeneratorState.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational" />
    <PackageReference Include="VistaDB.6" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Update="Properties\VistaDBStrings.Designer.tt">
      <Generator>TextTemplatingFileGenerator</Generator>
      <LastGenOutput>VistaDBStrings.Designer.cs</LastGenOutput>
      <CustomToolNamespace>Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.VistaDB.Internal</CustomToolNamespace>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Update="Properties\VistaDBStrings.Designer.cs">
      <DesignTime>True</DesignTime>
      <AutoGen>True</AutoGen>
      <DependentUpon>VistaDBStrings.Designer.tt</DependentUpon>
    </Compile>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
